# Arabic Formatting & Bidi Rules

When writing responses in Arabic mixed with English/Code:

1. Prefer not to bury long English paths or multi-token identifiers mid-sentence if they break text direction.
2. Short technical terms and file names **may** appear inline inside backticks when they stay readable (e.g. راجع `term_engine.py`). Longer paths, multi-line snippets, and command blocks go on their own lines or inside fenced code blocks.
3. Format numbered lists cleanly: write the number followed by standard English punctuation or bullet points without trailing inline English that flips the line.
4. Use Markdown tables when comparing terms or presenting technical parameters to ensure strict left-to-right/right-to-left layout separation.
